@@ -15,3 +15,33 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## SMS sign-up verification
+
+Set `TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID`, `TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN`, and `TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER` in the
+server environment (see `.env.example`). The sender must be authorized to send
+SMS to the destination country; trial accounts may require verified recipients.
+Without credentials the form reports that SMS verification is unavailable.
+No mock code is accepted and codes are never returned to the browser or logged.
+
+The same-origin `api/signup` endpoint sends a cryptographically random six-digit
+code through Twilio. The server session stores its SHA-256 hash, destination,
+10-minute expiry, 30-second resend cooldown, and five-attempt limit. Registration
+is forwarded to the existing account service only after the server checks the
+code. The verified phone number is included in the registration payload.
+
+SMS messages end with `@hostname #code`, using the request hostname without a
+scheme or port. Deploy behind a trusted proxy that preserves the public host,
+and use HTTPS for WebOTP in production. The client starts a feature-detected
+WebOTP listener before requesting delivery; it cancels on submission, resend,
+changing details, timeout, and unmount. Native one-time-code autofill and manual
+entry remain available. Registration and code delivery require a working Astro
+session store; use a shared persistent session driver for multiple server replicas.
+For production, add deployment-level per-IP and per-phone SMS rate limits across
+sessions to protect the messaging quota from clients creating new sessions.
+
+Run server verification tests without sending real SMS:
+
+```sh
+pnpm dlx tsx --test tests/signup.test.ts
+```
